 information about\nhealth impacts and how ozone pollution forms in Colorado, visit:\nhttps://cdphe.colorado.gov/ozone-pollution-and-your-health\n\nHEALTH INFORMATION...Increasing likelihood of respiratory symptoms\nand breathing discomfort in active children and adults and people\nwith lung disease, such as asthma. Active children and adults, and\npeople with lung disease, such as asthma, should reduce prolonged\nor heavy outdoor exertion.","ends":"2026-08-19T16:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Broomfield, CO; Boulder, CO; Douglas, CO; Larimer, CO; Jefferson, CO; Weld, CO; Denver, CO; Adams, CO; Arapahoe, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.bcd88b1b66192e2d43a08e5556c874386ead632c.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.bcd88b1b66192e2d43a08e5556c874386ead632c.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-19T07:50:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 190750 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 150 AM MDT Wed Aug 19 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Isolated storms again for Wednesday, though chances of stronger storms shift to the south. - Warming and drying trend to end the week, before monsoon moisture attempts to return Sunday into early next week. && .DISCUSSION /Through Tuesday/... Issued at 140","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-18T18:40:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Rest of today through Wednesday...Isolated to scattered showers and thunderstorms are expected this afternoon, mainly across the northeastern plains. Variable and gusty outflow winds will be possible with any convection that develops, with a few of the stronger storms producing some briefly heavy rainfall. Temperatures this afternoon will be near or a little above normal, with humidi","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"cht01","stati